{
  "id": "combination-sum-ii",
  "questionId": "combination-sum-ii",
  "slug": "combination-sum-ii",
  "title": "Combination Sum II",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Backtracking",
  "patterns": [
    "backtracking"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "sort the candidates first - this puts duplicate values next to each other and lets you process values from smallest to largest",
    "recurse with (start index, remaining target), trying each candidate from start onward and moving to start = i + 1 on the recursive call, since each item can only be used once",
    "prune two ways: stop trying further candidates at this position once candidates[i] alone exceeds the remaining target (sorted order makes this a clean early exit), and record a combination when remaining hits exactly 0",
    "to avoid duplicate combinations, at each recursion level skip a candidate if it equals the previous candidate you already tried at that same level - this is the same trick as Subsets II, applied to a sum-target search"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "using start = i (allowing reuse) instead of start = i + 1, which is the Combination Sum I behavior and violates 'use each item once'",
    "skipping duplicate values globally rather than only within the same recursion level, which incorrectly removes valid combinations like [1, 1, 6]",
    "not sorting first, which breaks both the duplicate-skipping logic and the early-exit pruning"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of positive integers, `candidates`, that may contain\nduplicate values, and a `target` number. Each element may be used at most\nonce per combination, even if the same value appears more than once in\nthe input, each occurrence is a separate usable item.\n\n**Return every unique combination of values from `candidates` that sums exactly to `target`.**\n\nNo two combinations in the result should share the same multiset of values.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= candidates.length <= 100",
      "1 <= candidates[i] <= 50",
      "1 <= target <= 30"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "many repeated values that must not produce duplicate combinations in the output",
      "no combination sums exactly to target (answer is empty)",
      "the only valid combination uses every single element"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
